# Emulator-only secret overrides (dotenv format), read ONLY by the Firebase
# Functions emulator (`firebase emulators:exec`). See firebase-tools
# functionsEmulator.js `resolveSecretEnvs`.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — CI stability:
# Every secret-declaring function (feedback-reportIssue, onClientErrorReport,
# onServerErrorReport, onSignInFailure, syncTrafikverket) declares a secret via
# defineSecret(). On each such function's cold start the emulator resolves its
# secrets, and for any secret NOT overridden here it makes a BLOCKING HTTPS call
# to Google Secret Manager (`secretmanager.googleapis.com`). On a CI runner that
# call can hang (no route / no credentials / slow metadata lookup), which stalls
# the runtime worker so the callable never returns — surfacing as
# "feedback-reportIssue timed out in 60000ms", the "Failed to handle request …
# Failed to load function" teardown noise, and the whole-suite freeze. Providing
# the keys here makes the emulator use these values directly and skip Secret
# Manager entirely.
#
# The override is only skipped for FALSY values, so these must be NON-EMPTY
# (see the `.filter((s) => !secretEnvs[s.key])` in resolveSecretEnvs). They are
# NON-SECRET placeholders — never real credentials. The GitHub token never
# reaches api.github.com: createGitHubIssue short-circuits in the emulator
# (process.env.FUNCTIONS_EMULATOR === 'true'), so the suite stays hermetic and
# still records githubIssueStatus:'failed', exactly as when no token was set.
#
# Deploys never ship this file: firebase.json's functions `ignore` excludes
# "*.local".
GITHUB_ISSUE_TOKEN=emulator-placeholder-not-a-real-token
TRAFIKVERKET_API_KEY=emulator-placeholder-not-a-real-key
